 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "Full Actors-pattern implementation (Governor + MarketEntry-LLM mock advisor + langgraph-clj StateGraph + append-only audit ledger + MemStore/DatomicStore via langchain-store.core) for the Democratic Republic of the Congo (COD -- NOT the Republic of Congo/Congo-Brazzaville, ISO code COG, a separate country with its own separate ARMP-acronymed regulator at armp.cg; do not conflate, see README.md and src/culture/facts.cljc): src/marketentry/{facts,governor,registry,store,marketentryllm,operation,phase,sim}.cljc + full test suite (governor contract, store contract MemStore≡DatomicStore parity, registry pure-function incl. Art. 37 preference-tier recompute, phase, facts) + docs/business-model.md + docs/operator-guide.md. The jurisdiction dossier (marketentry.facts) is grounded in a deep primary-source research pass (Loi n°10/010 du 27 avril 2010 relative aux marchés publics, its own PDF text downloaded from armp-rdc.cd and read in full; Décret n°12/045 du 1er novembre 2012 creating the Guichet Unique de Création d'Entreprise (GUCE); DGI's own site for the Numéro d'Identification Fiscale (NIF); OHADA accession record) and correctly rejects this repo's own original scaffold's mistaken 'ARMP / COREF' pairing (COREF is a real body but a broader public-finance-reform coordinator, not the procurement regulator -- ARMP alone, grounded in Loi n°10/010 Art. 14, is). The governor is SEVEN checks (not six): COD genuinely grounds TWO distinct jurisdiction-specific hard checks -- preference-tier-mismatch (the flagship check, an independently-recomputed ranked 6-tier classification under Loi n°10/010 Art. 37's national/regional preference, a check SHAPE new to this actor family) and nif-unverified (DGI's NIF, independently confirmed as DGI-mandated) -- the same seven-check shape as cloud-itonami-iso3166-mli's RCCM-entity-missing + nif-unverified combination, not the six-check shape of gnb/stp/sdn (whose dossiers each grounded only one jurisdiction-specific hard check). This follow-up migrated DatomicStore off a hand-rolled enc/dec* codec onto langchain-store.core (ADR-2607141600), fixed a docstring bug in marketentry.governor that undercounted the check total as six when the code already concatenated seven hard-violation functions, and added .github/workflows/ci.yml (sibling-checkout pattern, previously absent)."
